= Hello, Mosaic

This file is a placeholder so the project layout is exercisable
once the parser lands in MVP 0. See `manifest.md` §2 for the syntax
this is sketching toward.

The renderer now supports PDF WinAnsi text plus every glyph
the Adobe Core 14 fonts carry beyond WinAnsi via per-document
/Differences encodings: café culture, §1 legal citations, German
Straße addresses, ¶ pilcrows, © copyright marks, curly "smart"
quotes, Polish Łódź, Czech Příliš žluťoučký kůň, Hungarian árvíz-
tűrő, Romanian mâine. Math operators (≤ ≥ ≠ √ ∂ ∑ −) and the
fi/fl ligatures round out the set. Scripts without Core 14
glyphs (Cyrillic, CJK, Greek) still substitute with `?` and warn
until full font embedding lands (issue #9).
